<title>ITALY: Italy's Milan sees Feb CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</title>
<headline>Italy's Milan sees Feb CPI at 0.0 pct mo/mo.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Milan said its February consumer price index stood at 0.0 percent month-on-month and 2.4 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In January, Milan's inflation rate was 0.2 percent and 2.8 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Milan is one of 11 Italian cities to publish inflation data on Thursday and Friday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 19.1 percent on the national index. The 11 sample cities have a combined weighting of 75.66 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to January 1997):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.0    (0.2)    2.4  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Food				 -0.4   (-0.2)    1.2  (2.2)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.2    (0.1)    3.8  (3.9)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges  -1.8    (1.9)    7.6  (9.4)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.5    (0.0)    2.2  (2.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.6    (2.1)    3.5  (3.3)</p>
<p>    Transportation		    0.0   (-0.7)    0.8  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.3   (-0.7)    0.4  (0.8)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.2    (0.0)    4.2  (4.1)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.5    (0.9)    3.3  (3.7)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.5    (0.0)    1.3  (1.4)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom +392 66129526</p>
</text>
